{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Took the execution route the paused question already names rather than re-reading the launcher. A focused harness re-executes the test binary as a child with a marker variable, has the child launch a worker through the same syncutil stopper constructor and RunWorker call the engine uses for its snapshot workers, panics inside that worker with a fixed sentinel, and has the parent report whether the worker started, whether the child survived, whether the panic appears in the child's output, and the child's exit code, with spawn failure reported as a distinct event. Because the child is a separate process the parent's receipt survives even though the child does not, which is what makes the termination observable. A local run of the same harness recorded worker_started=true, survived=false, panicked=true, exit_code=2; the experiment is submitted for the retained receipt and the interpretation follows it.\"}"}}
